# systemd user-unit preset for middle-drag-gestures.
#
# Fedora ships 99-default-disable.preset containing a bare `disable *`, and
# %systemd_user_post runs `systemctl --global preset` through
# systemd-update-helper.  Without this file the answer is always "disabled",
# so every account had to run `systemctl --user enable` by hand - the package
# looked installed but dead, which is exactly what a user sees as "it does
# not work".
#
# With it, preset --global creates
#   /etc/systemd/user/graphical-session.target.wants/middle-drag-daemon.service
# for every account: the daemon starts at the next login, and can be started
# right now in the current session with
#   systemctl --user start middle-drag-daemon.service
#
# The 50- prefix sorts ahead of Fedora's 90-* and 99-* presets, and systemd
# takes the first matching entry, so `enable` here wins over `disable *`.
enable middle-drag-daemon.service
